 ## Retries
 
-A capture that times out is tried again, up to 3 attempts in all, one after the other.
+A capture that raises `GatewayTimeout` is tried again, up to 5 attempts in all (the initial call and 4 retries).
+`ATTEMPTS` and `BACKOFF_SECONDS` in `larder/capture.py` set the limit and the growing pauses: 2, 4, 6 and 8 seconds
+before the successive retries. A successful attempt returns immediately; a fifth timeout is raised to the caller.
+The pauses add up to 20 seconds of waiting on the confirmation page, in addition to time spent in gateway calls.
+
+Previously, 3 attempts ran back to back and could all hit the gateway's Friday 17:00–19:00 slowdown. One Friday left
+58 confirmed pantry orders for a volunteer to capture by hand. A sandbox replay with the new spacing would have
+captured 57 of those 58. The longer confirmation wait was accepted to reduce that manual work; switching gateways
+was ruled out because the contract runs to December 2026. See [issue 40](../../notes/issue-40.md) for the discussion.
 
